WEBVTT

00:04.270 --> 00:07.440
The shining time...

00:08.610 --> 00:16.160
...I have always imagined.

00:25.120 --> 00:30.250
Something will change tomorrow.

00:32.340 --> 00:38.640
I can sense it.

00:39.810 --> 00:46.940
In a mirage, I wait until you come.

00:47.190 --> 00:54.860
I walk briskly through the brightly lit streets.

00:55.780 --> 01:01.870
You've run so far.

01:02.950 --> 01:10.130
So I felt the air of your love.

01:10.340 --> 01:16.340
Soon after I see you,

01:17.680 --> 01:23.640
my stolen heart beats.

01:51.290 --> 01:53.130
<i>It's over?!</i>

01:53.130 --> 01:54.710
<i>Where are you going?</i>

01:54.710 --> 01:56.380
<i>Give it up!</i>

01:56.380 --> 01:58.590
<i>What about Maron?!</i>

01:58.590 --> 02:00.220
<i>I'll come pick her up.</i>

02:00.220 --> 02:03.260
<i>Lies! You don't even want to...</i>

02:03.260 --> 02:05.310
<i>Calm down.</i>

02:05.310 --> 02:07.850
<i>I will come pick her up. I promise.</i>

02:15.190 --> 02:17.950
<i>Noooooo!</i>

02:20.200 --> 02:22.780
Maron? Maron?!

02:26.580 --> 02:29.080
She's still asleep!

02:31.960 --> 02:34.590
Maron! Wake up, Maron!

02:34.590 --> 02:36.550
Miyako-chan has come to pick you up!

02:36.550 --> 02:38.170
Come on, Maron!

02:39.590 --> 02:41.590
Maron! Maron!!

02:41.590 --> 02:43.810
She's probably in a foul mood.

02:43.810 --> 02:48.310
Geez! If you won't come out, I'll go to school with Chiaki without you!

02:48.310 --> 02:49.600
Is that what you want?!

02:50.650 --> 02:52.940
Geez, we're going to be late. Let's go, Chiaki!

02:57.740 --> 03:01.070
<i>"I will come pick her up..."  was it?</i>

03:01.070 --> 03:02.570
Maron...

03:03.530 --> 03:06.700
It was just a dream. Let's eat breakfast!

03:06.700 --> 03:07.290
Are you sure?

03:07.290 --> 03:10.830
WHAT?! I'm late! This is bad!

03:11.580 --> 03:13.290
Someone help me!

03:13.630 --> 03:20.260
Forget-Me-Not Heart Thief

03:25.260 --> 03:27.010
<i>What an awful dream...</i>

03:43.240 --> 03:44.280
- Good morning!

03:51.750 --> 03:54.250
What's up with the gloomy face?

03:54.250 --> 03:55.290
Good morning.

03:58.420 --> 04:00.420
Here, take this.

04:00.420 --> 04:02.010
Um, this is...?

04:02.010 --> 04:03.890
It's a forget-me-not flower.

04:03.890 --> 04:09.060
Soon it will bloom and brighten up that gloomy face!

04:10.270 --> 04:10.810
But...

04:10.810 --> 04:15.270
The bud is still hard, but as long as you believe that it will bloom, it will.

04:15.270 --> 04:17.230
Okay, line up!

04:17.230 --> 04:19.110
I don't want any money.

04:19.110 --> 04:22.450
I just want the flower to bloom all across the town!

04:22.450 --> 04:25.030
Can I really have this?

04:25.030 --> 04:27.780
It's okay. Please take it.

04:27.780 --> 04:32.960
When that flower blooms, Yurika-chan's boyfriend is going to come pick her up.

04:32.960 --> 04:37.540
So please take it home and make it bloom.

04:37.540 --> 04:41.170
She's going to act like this for a while, so go ahead and take it.

04:41.170 --> 04:42.840
Oji-san, did you say something?

04:41.170 --> 04:45.050
Oji-san = Old man

04:42.840 --> 04:45.050
Nothing at all.

04:45.050 --> 04:47.550
Thank you! I'll take good care of it!

04:47.550 --> 04:49.510
Give it enough water, okay? Here you go.

04:49.510 --> 04:51.640
Take good care of it...

04:51.640 --> 04:53.390
...and there's no need to pay me.

05:05.240 --> 05:06.610
I must somehow avoid being...

05:13.080 --> 05:14.290
Out!

05:14.290 --> 05:16.040
Darn!

05:16.040 --> 05:19.590
It's the second time this week. Stand outside!

05:19.590 --> 05:20.250
Yes, ma'am.

05:20.250 --> 05:22.920
Wait. Give me the flower.

05:22.920 --> 05:23.710
Yes, ma'am.

05:24.550 --> 05:28.220
The poor thing needs some sunlight.

05:28.220 --> 05:32.930
Idiot. I went to wake you up, but you had to go buy some flower.

05:32.930 --> 05:34.850
Someone gave it to me!

05:35.980 --> 05:37.060
Gave?

05:37.560 --> 05:41.610
Some wimpy guy, giving Maron a flower?

05:42.070 --> 05:46.490
So?! It was someone a lot nicer than you!

05:46.490 --> 05:48.910
Kusakabe? Out!

05:48.910 --> 05:49.950
Yes, ma'am.

05:51.080 --> 05:55.870
I think, in the language of flowers, the forget-me-not means "true love."

06:01.290 --> 06:05.800
So, her boyfriend will come back when that flower blooms?

06:05.800 --> 06:09.260
What a romantic story!

06:09.260 --> 06:12.600
Yeah, but what an irresponsible promise.

06:12.600 --> 06:16.560
Flowers bloom at different times.

06:17.520 --> 06:21.520
Chiaki, you'll never understand what it's like to wait.

06:21.520 --> 06:23.980
I don't want to know.

06:25.530 --> 06:28.110
Hey! What do you mean there's no letter?

06:28.110 --> 06:31.660
It didn't come yesterday or the day before. Hand it over!

06:31.660 --> 06:33.450
Hurry up and give it to me!

06:33.450 --> 06:36.000
Is she the one you were talking about?

06:36.000 --> 06:37.910
What's happening?

06:37.910 --> 06:42.130
Hey, I have to stop this! This is clearly an act of violence.

06:42.130 --> 06:45.670
You do have it, right? Get it out, now!

06:46.090 --> 06:47.380
Assault...

06:48.090 --> 06:49.840
If you don't...

06:50.720 --> 06:52.050
Making threats...

06:52.720 --> 06:54.760
I'll cut off your neck!

06:56.220 --> 06:58.100
Attempted murder...

06:58.640 --> 07:01.810
Okay, out of my way, move it!

07:04.070 --> 07:05.440
What are you looking at?

07:05.440 --> 07:06.900
Mind your own business!

07:26.090 --> 07:28.630
Is she really the one who gave you that flower?

07:30.090 --> 07:32.590
Sir, did something happen?

07:32.590 --> 07:35.100
Oh, you're the girl from this morning.

07:35.930 --> 07:38.930
Another day went by without a letter from her boyfriend.

07:38.930 --> 07:41.730
But, I thought when this flower blooms...

07:41.730 --> 07:47.730
Yes, her boyfriend went to Paris, hoping to become a painter.

07:47.730 --> 07:55.160
He promised he'd return on the third spring when all the forget-me-nots bloom.

07:55.160 --> 07:57.450
And that's this year, right?

07:57.450 --> 08:00.830
Yes, but the flowers are about to bloom...

08:00.830 --> 08:04.790
...and no one knows if he truly will return.

08:04.790 --> 08:06.090
But that's...

08:07.290 --> 08:09.090
Maron, let's go home.

08:09.090 --> 08:11.970
Uh, I just remembered I have something to do.

08:11.970 --> 08:13.680
Go home without me.

08:13.680 --> 08:14.680
Maron...

08:15.680 --> 08:17.050
Leave her alone.

08:17.930 --> 08:20.140
Let's go home together.

08:20.140 --> 08:20.640
Okay!

08:24.810 --> 08:27.650
Excuse me, where does the flower seller live?

08:52.880 --> 08:55.430
They're all forget-me-nots!

08:59.760 --> 09:04.480
Um, this flower will bloom if I trust in it, right?

09:05.940 --> 09:08.940
Am I an idiot? Am I childish?

09:10.610 --> 09:15.030
I believed that when the forget-me-nots were about to bloom, a letter from him would arrive.

09:15.030 --> 09:17.280
And that when they bloomed,

09:17.280 --> 09:21.620
he would walk up that path to meet me.

09:25.290 --> 09:30.540
I'm sure he will come when they bloom, so please believe in him.

09:30.540 --> 09:32.000
You're right.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.800
Since the buds are large,

09:34.800 --> 09:38.890
I should make them bloom all over town and meet him when he comes.

09:54.690 --> 09:56.950
If I believe and wait...

10:02.870 --> 10:03.990
Chiaki?

10:05.330 --> 10:07.670
<i>"This ain't like you at all, baby."</i>

10:07.670 --> 10:09.580
What is <i>this</i>?!

10:09.580 --> 10:13.920
<i>"It's not cool to just wait for a letter every day."</i>

10:14.840 --> 10:17.760
<i>Forget that guy who can't even send you a letter.</i>

10:17.760 --> 10:20.340
<i>Open the window and look outside. It's such a bright day.</i>

10:20.340 --> 10:22.930
What's with him, acting like he knows me!

10:26.100 --> 10:28.850
He's right, it's sunny.

10:29.400 --> 10:31.110
Isn't it?

10:31.110 --> 10:32.310
Chiaki!

10:32.310 --> 10:37.650
Did you actually wait there until I came home?

10:37.650 --> 10:38.740
Yeah.

10:38.740 --> 10:41.410
Isn't that like...stalking?

10:41.410 --> 10:44.910
I just came out because I heard you open the window.

10:44.910 --> 10:50.000
Yeah, sure. Don't put weird letters in my mailbox anymore, okay?

10:51.540 --> 10:54.380
Hey, whose letters are you waiting for?

10:54.380 --> 10:56.130
None of your business.

10:56.130 --> 10:58.050
Is it your lover or something like that?

10:58.050 --> 11:01.010
If you want to think that, go ahead!

11:03.510 --> 11:05.930
Damn, she's so stubborn...

11:07.310 --> 11:09.980
Notice

11:07.310 --> 11:09.980
Don't go away!

11:07.310 --> 11:09.980
I'll return right after these messages!

11:07.310 --> 11:09.980
Kaitou Jeanne

11:10.900 --> 11:13.480
Notice

11:10.900 --> 11:13.480
I'm back to continue my adventures

11:10.900 --> 11:13.480
Kaitou Jeanne

11:23.280 --> 11:24.580
Hey, you over there!

11:24.580 --> 11:26.120
Get rid of that gloomy face!

11:26.120 --> 11:27.450
And take this.

11:27.830 --> 11:30.710
You too, here you go.

11:30.710 --> 11:31.870
Good morning.

11:33.670 --> 11:36.420
Here you go! Make it bloom.

11:36.420 --> 11:39.510
She was so down yesterday.

11:39.510 --> 11:41.930
I don't understand women.

11:41.930 --> 11:45.260
Chiaki, you'll never understand women in your lifetime.

11:45.260 --> 11:47.970
Hey, Maron, let's go. We'll be late.

11:51.310 --> 11:52.810
Hey, wait up!

12:03.280 --> 12:06.280
<i>Please make the letter come.</i>

12:13.120 --> 12:17.960
Toudaiji! Is Nagoya's face more entertaining than my lessons?!

12:17.960 --> 12:19.090
Eh?

12:19.090 --> 12:20.670
Out!

12:31.680 --> 12:33.310
What's wrong?

12:33.310 --> 12:35.100
Nothing, just looking around.

12:35.100 --> 12:36.560
Huh? Where's Maron?

12:36.560 --> 12:37.650
Didn't come.

12:37.650 --> 12:42.320
I see. Miyako, can I talk to you after practice?

12:42.320 --> 12:45.860
Of course! Just wait. Practice will be over soon.

12:45.860 --> 12:47.320
Yay!

13:11.270 --> 13:14.980
Whatever's in the letter... It's not my fault!

13:14.980 --> 13:16.020
So long!

13:19.770 --> 13:23.740
<i>"To Yurika, be prepared to go to Paris."</i>

13:23.740 --> 13:25.740
<i>"I'll pick you up soon."</i>

13:25.740 --> 13:27.910
It's here! It's finally here, Oji-san!

13:29.070 --> 13:31.370
You must be so happy, Yurika-chan!

13:31.370 --> 13:33.080
I told you...

13:33.080 --> 13:34.830
...that he would come back to me.

13:36.210 --> 13:39.540
It's a picture of a forget-me-not. He must have drawn it.

13:39.540 --> 13:40.750
What, really?

13:45.720 --> 13:47.630
He is a really good artist.

13:47.630 --> 13:49.010
It's really good.

13:55.600 --> 13:56.890
What's wrong?

14:00.650 --> 14:02.690
Hey, Yurika-chan!

14:11.740 --> 14:13.040
What happened?!

14:13.830 --> 14:15.200
I don't know.

14:15.200 --> 14:18.370
She was so happy because of the letter, but suddenly...

14:20.710 --> 14:23.880
I love this bridge.

14:23.880 --> 14:27.300
It's so romantic.

14:27.300 --> 14:29.220
Yeah, it feels good.

14:30.140 --> 14:32.220
Anyway, what did you want to talk to me about?

14:32.220 --> 14:33.350
Well...

14:33.350 --> 14:34.970
What?

14:34.970 --> 14:39.310
Whose letter is Maron waiting for?

14:40.650 --> 14:41.690
You know, don't you?

14:41.690 --> 14:45.940
You brought me here to ask that?

14:45.940 --> 14:48.610
You're the one who brought me here.

14:48.610 --> 14:50.360
Well, can you tell me?

14:52.320 --> 14:53.870
Probably her boyfriend.

14:57.620 --> 14:58.790
Just as I thought.

14:59.080 --> 15:01.290
We're in big trouble!

15:01.630 --> 15:03.960
Maron, open the window!

15:04.590 --> 15:06.550
Man, that was close!

15:06.550 --> 15:09.930
If I'm seen here, she'll find out that Chiaki is Sinbad.

15:11.300 --> 15:13.760
Maron! A Demon! I found a Demon!

15:13.760 --> 15:17.020
Yeah, yeah. Is that all you can say?

15:17.020 --> 15:19.230
This isn't the time for that!

15:19.230 --> 15:22.060
We have to go seal it now!

15:22.060 --> 15:27.650
It seems to have a lot of power so the flower lady might die if we don't take care of it!

15:27.650 --> 15:31.610
Flower lady? That lady who comes to town to sell flowers?

15:31.610 --> 15:32.910
That's right!

15:32.910 --> 15:35.580
So, what time did you put on the notice?

15:35.580 --> 15:39.160
Four o' clock. It's still early but her life is...

15:40.120 --> 15:41.500
She's in a hurry...

15:46.210 --> 15:49.970
Yes... That flower lady in town...

15:49.970 --> 15:51.220
Yes.. I'll leave it up to you.

15:51.220 --> 15:52.930
What did Miyako-san say?

15:52.930 --> 15:54.850
She's all fired up.

15:54.850 --> 15:57.850
She says she'll completely destroy Jeanne.

15:57.850 --> 16:00.730
Sounds like she's in a blood-thirsty mood...

16:04.400 --> 16:06.060
Fin, please.

16:06.060 --> 16:07.270
Okay.

16:13.280 --> 16:15.030
<i>Jeanne d'Arc, lend me your power.</i>

16:25.830 --> 16:27.750
<i>Strong and serious...</i>

16:27.750 --> 16:29.500
<i>Matchless and marvelous...</i>

16:29.500 --> 16:31.130
<i>Energetic and courageous!</i>

16:34.380 --> 16:35.180
What's that?

16:35.180 --> 16:36.510
What's going on?

16:43.060 --> 16:43.850
Point A?

16:44.480 --> 16:45.850
Everything's ready.

16:46.900 --> 16:47.980
<i>Point B?</i>

16:47.980 --> 16:49.320
Anytime.

16:50.070 --> 16:51.110
Point C?

16:51.110 --> 16:52.240
<i>Okay.</i>

16:52.240 --> 16:53.400
Point D?

16:53.400 --> 16:54.650
<i>All ready.</i>

16:55.280 --> 17:00.700
As the police, we must not be thwarted in our efforts to apprehend Jeanne this time!

17:00.700 --> 17:01.660
Dad?

17:01.660 --> 17:05.080
<i>Don't worry. We have enough people on guard.</i>

17:05.080 --> 17:07.500
<i>Jeanne will be trapped like a rat.</i>

17:07.500 --> 17:10.590
Okay! Come if you will, Jeanne!

17:11.340 --> 17:13.550
Jeanne, there are too many guards!

17:13.550 --> 17:14.630
What should we do?

17:15.800 --> 17:16.840
I'll make it work.

17:16.840 --> 17:22.020
I won't ever forgive the Demon that tries to trample on Yurika-san's feelings after she finally got that letter!

17:22.020 --> 17:23.810
I'm going to destroy it!

17:29.440 --> 17:30.940
Sinbad? Where is he?

17:33.360 --> 17:35.570
Akita-san! Haruta-san!

17:35.570 --> 17:36.530
What's going on?

17:42.870 --> 17:44.000
What the...?

17:47.210 --> 17:49.290
Sinbad has arrived.

17:49.290 --> 17:51.290
Natsuda-san, now!

17:51.290 --> 17:53.090
Shoot the net bazooka!

17:54.760 --> 17:55.380
Damn it!

18:00.220 --> 18:02.060
Wait, we haven't caught Jeanne yet!

18:06.310 --> 18:07.600
It's Jeanne!

18:19.990 --> 18:21.950
She's stealing the entire car!

18:21.950 --> 18:23.120
Just as I planned.

18:24.620 --> 18:27.540
We've got her now.

18:27.540 --> 18:29.040
Fuyuta-san, it's time.

18:33.250 --> 18:35.090
The brakes don't work?!

18:35.090 --> 18:36.970
Jeanne, you're under arrest!

18:37.970 --> 18:40.930
W-Why is the car moving?

18:40.930 --> 18:43.390
Do something or we'll crash!

18:44.010 --> 18:47.890
"Do something?" Okay, I'll drive so just let me handle the car!

18:54.360 --> 18:55.780
Sinbad? How...?!

18:56.740 --> 19:01.110
It was easy getting out of that net. It's your turn now.

19:01.110 --> 19:02.450
Mine?

19:02.450 --> 19:03.410
There!

19:05.450 --> 19:07.580
The Petit Claire is not reacting to the Demon!

19:07.580 --> 19:10.370
The letter must be at her house.

19:10.370 --> 19:12.540
Damn, this must be a trap too!

19:12.540 --> 19:16.590
Dad, they're caught in the trap.

19:16.590 --> 19:18.090
<i>Catch them!</i>

19:18.090 --> 19:20.970
Right! Put up the roadblock!

19:32.230 --> 19:33.400
A barricade?

19:40.610 --> 19:42.110
Damn, we can't get through!

19:44.490 --> 19:45.780
Stop!

19:45.780 --> 19:48.750
Get out of my way! I'm in a hurry!

19:48.750 --> 19:51.460
Stop the car! This time we've lost!

19:52.710 --> 19:55.630
I can't lose! That letter just arrived!

19:55.630 --> 19:58.550
I won't forgive the Demon for possessing that letter!

19:59.460 --> 20:01.340
Stop it! You're going to die!

20:01.340 --> 20:02.840
I won't!

20:02.840 --> 20:09.220
Until I get a letter from Mom and Dad, I refuse to die!

20:10.350 --> 20:12.390
Stop! You're going to hit us!

20:12.390 --> 20:14.060
It's no use! Jump out!

20:14.060 --> 20:16.230
I can't lose!

20:28.950 --> 20:30.830
How the hell...?!

20:38.670 --> 20:40.340
Get out of my way!

20:44.800 --> 20:46.390
Yurika-san!

20:52.480 --> 20:53.810
I'll help you.

20:53.810 --> 20:56.770
I'll let the forget-me-nots bloom!

20:56.770 --> 20:58.730
In the name of God...

20:58.730 --> 21:01.360
You, a Demon, born in darkness...

21:02.900 --> 21:04.450
I seal you here!

21:05.030 --> 21:06.660
<i>Checkmate!</i>

21:18.590 --> 21:19.670
Yurika-san!

21:26.720 --> 21:28.550
The flowers are...

21:28.550 --> 21:30.430
The forget-me-nots are...

21:34.310 --> 21:37.060
He's coming! He's coming to get me!

21:51.120 --> 21:54.080
If you believe in it, it will come true.

22:05.470 --> 22:11.300
For billions of years,

22:11.390 --> 22:20.860
it kept infinite thoughts.

22:23.020 --> 22:29.490
It wakens the memory of the distant past.

22:29.740 --> 22:35.790
A life born in the wild ocean.

22:36.410 --> 22:39.210
The huge mountains...

22:41.920 --> 22:48.840
...emitted white smoke and covered the Sun.

22:49.340 --> 22:53.890
It took everything.

22:56.140 --> 23:02.110
On the deserted land with you,

23:02.190 --> 23:09.110
we watched the world ending...

23:09.320 --> 23:15.160
Someday we'll go beyond space-time...

23:15.290 --> 23:24.960
and I'll wish to meet you again.

23:31.510 --> 23:34.100
Wow, what a beautiful dress!

23:34.100 --> 23:37.430
When I get married, I want to wear a dress like this too...

23:37.430 --> 23:39.100
I wonder what Chiaki will think about it...

23:39.100 --> 23:41.730
Ehh... Are you gonna quit being a detective?

23:41.730 --> 23:48.860
Like I said... Getting married with someone you love, having children, having the warmth of a family...

23:48.860 --> 23:50.740
Working hard as a detective!!!

23:50.740 --> 23:52.110
Miyako?

23:52.110 --> 23:55.620
Kamikaze Kaitou Jeanne: The Target Is the Wedding Dress

23:55.620 --> 23:59.960
I, Miyako Toudaiji, will not forgive those who trample on love!
